# Line endings, fixed rather than guessed.
#
# core.autocrlf leaves the working tree CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux, so the
# same commit packs to two different XPIs depending on who built it. That makes
# a published checksum unverifiable: a user cannot rebuild and compare, and CI
# cannot confirm a local build. eol=lf pins the working tree on every platform,
# so the bytes that go into the archive depend on the commit and nothing else.
#
# Zotero reads all of these through its own loaders, none of which care about
# line endings, and the PowerShell dev scripts parse LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for everything the XPI is built from, so a future .gitattributes
# edit cannot quietly drop one of them back to native endings.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.ftl   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf

# Built artifacts. Not tracked today, but never diff or normalize one.
*.xpi   binary
